WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.369
Three House committees

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:05.372
are currently investigating the border

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.707
as a possible prelude

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.476
to impeaching you

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.745
as secretary of Homeland Security.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:14.881
Here is House Speaker Kevin McCarthy.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:15.782
Take a look.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.487
I am calling on the secretary to resign

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.757
He cannot

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:26.192
and must not remain in that position.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.462
If Secretary

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.798
Mayorkas does not resign,

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.101
House Republicans will investigate.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.504
Every order, every action

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:41.341
and every failure will determine

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.911
whether we can begin impeachment inquiry.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.715
If House Republicans go ahead,

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.384
you could be the first Cabinet secretary

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:55.021
to be impeached since 1876.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.524
How seriously do you take these calls?

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.858
For your impeachment.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.261
Oh, I take them. I take them seriously.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.930
It is, it is the leadership

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.866
of the House that provided those remarks.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.837
I don't dismiss it by by any measure,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.773
but what I do is I focus on my work.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.876
What do you think is the basis

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.378
for their calling for your impeachment?

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.779
Do you think you've done anything wrong?

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:20.413
No, I don't.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.783
I think it is a disagreement over policy,

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.218
and I think it is used

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.187
for political purposes.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:31.091
To continue a negative dialog

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.959
about a migration challenge

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.061
that is not unique to the United States.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.263
To continue that dialog to uplift it

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.865
for political reasons.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:39.599
So, Mr.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:39.999
Secretary,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.701
have you come to a conclusion

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.770
if these House committees

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.140
either request you or subpoena you

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.343
as part of either the investigation

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.878
or an impeachment proceeding,

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.113
have you decided whether or not

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.381
you will appear before those committees?

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.983
I intend to appear

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.119
when Congress calls me to do so.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.854
House Republicans

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:03.823
say that you have repeatedly lied

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.992
to Congress when you have said this

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:06.459
take a lot

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.530
The border is closed.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.365
The border is secure.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:15.001
The border is secure.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.370
Critics point out in 20, 20,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.306
Donald Trump's final year in office, U.S.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.674
border authorities

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:22.876
encountered migrants

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:25.712
458,000 times at the border.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.481
But under Joe Biden in 2022

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:32.085
there were 2.3 million encounters.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.287
How can you say the border is secure

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:34.954
right now

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:38.858
the United States has millions of jobs

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.028
opening due to the economic success

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.863
of this administration.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.633
We have progressed in conquering

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.234
the pandemic far

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.036
more than the countries

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.472
to the south of Mexico.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.008
And that makes the United States

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.544
an appealing place of destination

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:58.411
for people

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.846
fleeing persecution

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.114
or otherwise in desperate

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.315
need of a better life.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.850
But when you say

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.118
what does secure mean to you,

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:05.919
it certainly doesn't mean

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:06.786
that people aren't able

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.088
to get across the border illegally.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.291
Of course not. That is that.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.091
By that measure,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.160
the border has never been secure. Right.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.429
Since the Department of Homeland

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.431
Security was created,

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.033
individuals have invaded.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.968
By what measure is it secure now, sir?

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.038
So there is not a common definition

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:26.105
of that.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:26.839
What's your article

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.540
What's your definition?

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.441
Our goal

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:29.209
is to achieve

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.411
operational control of the border,

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.580
to do everything that we can

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.782
to support our personnel

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:38.851
with the resources is the technology,

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.553
the policies

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.989
that really advance

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.958
the security of the border

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.826
and do not come

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.629
at the cost of the values of our country.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.464
But on the question of security.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.967
We have all seen the scenes of

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.603
of floods, of people walking across

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.239
shallow points in the Rio Grande.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:03:59.472
We've

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:02.809
all seen the pictures of encampments

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.143
in downtowns

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.679
in El Paso places in Arizona,

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.081
We've all seen the pictures

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.182
of the flood

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:09.916
of migrants

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.318
coming to New York by those standards.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.721
It is not a secure border.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:15.355
The vast

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.257
majority of those individuals

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.993
have not sought to evade law enforcement,

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.862
but have actually surrendered themselves

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.163
to law enforcement

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.732
and made a claim for relief

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.033
under our laws.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:31.037
The challenge the challenge is that

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:34.140
between that time of encounter

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.409
and the time of an ultimate

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.810
immigration judges,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.046
an evaluation of their claim

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.515
for asylum is four plus years.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:45.451
Critics say that when he took office,

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.186
President Biden

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.455
setting the policy view and forcing

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.857
the policy,

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.292
send a clear message

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.527
to prospective migrants.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.063
He ended enrollments in the program

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.231
that asylum seekers

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.600
had to remain in Mexico.

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.302
He wanted to stop using Title

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.336
42 public health

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.371
protections to expel migrants,

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.974
and he halted construction of the border

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:08.741
wall.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.244
Here is the chief patrol agent,

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.713
your employee for the Tucson sector.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.213
Take a look

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:16.382
in the

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:17.917
Tucson sector

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.086
interviewing people post-arrest.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.087
What what became

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.789
the most common response

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.357
was that they believed

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.025
that when the administration changed,

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:28.328
that the law changed and policy changed

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:31.698
and that there was an open border.

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:34.167
Migrants believe there's an open

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.835
border across

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:38.304
Have you heard some of our

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.807
political leaders speak about the border

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:43.843
and communicate that the border is open?

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:46.112
I don't think the more than

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.947
1.5 million people

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:48.881
who have been removed

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.750
or expelled from the border

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.485
would consider the border open.

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.620
But political leaders

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.556
communicate that the border is open,

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:59.392
that is music to the smugglers ears

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.994
and the smugglers themselves to spread.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:02.895
You're going to blame this

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.297
all on Republican website?

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.098
Not absolutely.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:05.865
You're not going to say

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.233
that the administration

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.168
and the policies on Remain in Mexico

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:10.403
are title 42

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.938
or stopping construction of the wall

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.473
that that had no impact.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:15.241
Chris, that's not what I said.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:17.610
I'm just I'm just citing for you

00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:20.313
a few things and please allow me.

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.416
Number one, they they use that rhetoric.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:24.283
Number two,

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.084
we're dealing

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.153
with smuggling organizations

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.222
that are far more sophisticated

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:30.590
than than they were

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.658
when I prosecuted them for 12 years

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.927
as an assistant United States Attorney

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:36.996
and as the United States attorney.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:39.165
They they spread disinformation.

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:42.268
They spread misinformation and the like.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.070
Let's talk a little bit about you

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.239
because your life story is wrapped up

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.408
in this whole question of migration.

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:50.576
Your family left Cuba

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.311
when you were a baby.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.280
I think you were one year old yes.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.249
And your mother, Anita,

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:58.317
was already a

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:59.352
refugee because

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:01.087
she had fled the Nazis

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.156
from Romania to go to Cuba

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:04.123
and then fled

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:06.092
Cuba to go to the United States with you

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:06.926
and your

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:10.263
and your family when Castro took over.

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:13.266
How does all of that history

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:15.468
shape your view of people

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:18.337
crossing borders to improve their lives

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.906
and escape violence?

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:22.475
My parents instilled in me

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:25.478
the profound meaning of displacement,

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.180
the yearning

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.849
to give one's children a better life

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:33.386
than what the life one

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.687
has had,

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:37.857
the fragility of life.

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:41.894
And so I understand deeply

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:45.331
the plight of individuals

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:47.800
who leave their homes,

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.969
whether they flee persecution

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.305
or aspire to a better life.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:55.341
We are a nation of immigrants.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.377
We are also a nation of laws.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.313
Those laws

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.448
provide for humanitarian relief

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:04.650
for those who qualify.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.486
They also provide

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:07.186
that individuals

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:09.755
who do not qualify will be removed.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.124
That's how that's how we do our work.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.826
In the Department of Homeland Security

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:14.927
and the slings

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:15.561
and arrows

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.697
of your critics on Capitol Hill.

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.232
Not going to force you out.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.600
They will not force me out.

